  "details": "a component, for avatars, that limits the range of movement that a bone can move in, exactly like final IKs bone rotation limiters\n\nFinal IK has this http://www.root-motion.com/finalikdox/html/page14.html\n\nI'll use a skirt as an example to try and explain the use for this. \n\nthe upper leg bone should be able to move in the following range where the skirt bones wouldn't move with upper leg bone. normally the skirt bones would follow the leg 1:1\n\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/387055787937234946/875160360200568922/unknown.png\n\nif you were able to limit the rotation range that a bone could move, you can constrain the skirt bones to the upper leg bone, then use a rotation limiter on the skirt bones to limit their range to just this\n\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/387055787937234946/875161473893171210/unknown.png\n\nhaving this would allow the leg to move up to this point\n\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/387055787937234946/875162985654550578/unknown.png\n\nbefore the skirt starts to rotate with the skirt \n\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/387055787937234946/875163385623355392/unknown.png\n\nthe problem with the final IK components is constraints over power it, so for avatars we would need a custom component to do something similar to the final IK components, but runs after constraints\n\n\nother examples of use cases:\n\narmor shoulder pad that stops going down with the arm after a certain point but will raise with the arm when the arm moved above a point\n\nany part of an outfit that would raise but not lower more then resting, shawls, most things around shoulder and neck\nwould be really useful for wider skirts or dresses so your legs can move freely under the skirt/dress",
